# Phase 1 package — manual-start end-to-end session daemon

## Intent

Deliver the smallest deployable process seam inside `@naxodev/music-core`: one foreground, Node-compatible daemon owns one real `createSystemMedia()` adapter, an Effect v4 coordinator, and a versioned newline-delimited JSON Unix-socket server. A public client connects to an explicitly supplied socket, receives provider status and replay/live state, and sends globally ordered transport commands.

This phase proves the end-to-end boundary with two clients but deliberately leaves both host packages on their current per-instance backend path. Automatic launch, reconnect, singleton/stale-socket recovery, and 20+ client hardening are Phase 2 work.

## Current source constraints to preserve

- `packages/music-core/system-media.ts` already owns provider detection, the independent playback clock, normalized stream snapshots, and the `media-control` stream restart sequence of 1/2/4/8 seconds capped at 8 seconds. Reuse one adapter instance; do not create a second clock/provider path in the session code.
- The host implementations currently contain the coalesced sample lane, stale-sample guards, 3/5/8-second dynamic poll, optimistic transport projection, and delayed reconciliation. Reproduce those rules in the coordinator without changing either host yet.
- `packages/music-core` currently publishes TypeScript source directly. Keep existing exports working and add the client surface without removing or renaming low-level provider/clock exports.
- The workspace already resolves `effect@4.0.0-beta.101` through `packages/apnea`, but `music-core` must declare it directly because its public runtime now imports Effect.
- `**/dist/` is ignored. Build and inspect `packages/music-core/dist/music-sessiond.js`, but do not add generated output to the worktree.

